{"name":"Mountain Bluebird","hex":"#4c98c2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mountain bluebird","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bluebird of species Sialia currucoides, found in eastern North America."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mountain_bluebird"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mountain bluebird","blocks":[{"text":"The mountain bluebird is a migratory small thrush that is found in mountainous districts of western North America. It has a light underbelly and black eyes. Adult males have thin bills and are bright turquoise-blue and somewhat lighter underneath. Adult females have duller blue wings and tail, grey breast, grey crown, throat and back. In fresh fall plumage, the female's throat and breast are tinged with red-orange which is brownish near the flank, contrasting with white tail underparts. Their call is a thin 'few' while their song is a warbled high 'chur chur'. The mountain bluebird is the state bird of Idaho and Nevada. This bird is an omnivore and it can live 6 to 10 years in the wild. It eats spiders, grasshoppers, flies and other insects, and small fruits. The mountain bluebird is a relative of the eastern and western bluebirds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Mountain_Bluebird.jpg/330px-Mountain_Bluebird.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_bluebird","wikidata":"Q819825"},{"title":"Mountain","blocks":[{"text":"A mountain is an elevated portion of the surface of a planet, generally with steep sides that show significant exposed bedrock. Although there are no universally accepted definitions, a mountain is usually considered higher than a hill. By definition, mountains are often thought of as being a landform which is higher than 2,000 feet (610 m). It may either have a limited summit area or be a smaller plateau with high elevation and steep sides. A few mountains are isolated summits, but most occur in mountain ranges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg/330px-Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain","wikidata":"Q8502"},{"title":"Bluebird","blocks":[{"text":"The bluebirds are a North American group of medium-sized, mostly insectivorous or omnivorous passerine birds in the genus Sialia of the thrush family (Turdidae)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Eastern_Bluebird%2C_crop.jpg/330px-Eastern_Bluebird%2C_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluebird","wikidata":"Q853286"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Sialia_currucoides_female.jpg/500px-Sialia_currucoides_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Sialia_currucoides_female.jpg/1280px-Sialia_currucoides_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Sialia_currucoides_female.jpg/500px-Sialia_currucoides_female.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASialia_currucoides_female.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Mountain_Bluebird%2C_Santa_Fe.jpg/500px-Mountain_Bluebird%2C_Santa_Fe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Mountain_Bluebird%2C_Santa_Fe.jpg/1280px-Mountain_Bluebird%2C_Santa_Fe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wiki